{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1 shell: implement on top of Spring Shell; invoke the s-c-d REST API using a HATEOAS-aware client (e.g., Spring HATEOAS Traverson over RestTemplate) so the shell follows links exposed by the server rather than hard-coding URIs.",
    "U7 stream REST support: implement a Spring MVC @RestController (StreamController) exposing HATEOAS resources for stream definition, deployment, undeployment, destruction, listing, and status; delegate to stream definition/deployment domain services; consistent error handling via @ControllerAdvice.",
    "U2 redis counter: port the Spring XD redis counter as a standalone Spring Boot application module using the spring-cloud-stream binder abstraction; Redis access via Spring Data Redis; module packaged per spring-cloud-stream-modules conventions.",
    "U5 bootified ModuleLauncher: convert ModuleLauncher to a Spring Boot application using auto-configuration and @ConfigurationProperties with relaxed binding for module/launch options, replacing ad-hoc argument parsing.",
    "U4 external module dependencies: extend the Boot loader approach (PropertiesLauncher-style) with a module resolver that resolves module-dependent JARs (e.g., JDBC drivers) from Maven repositories at launch time and places them on the launched module's classpath, keeping them out of the OOTB module archives.",
    "U6 PHD/HDFS: handle as a time-boxed investigation spike (classloader isolation options, dependency shading vs. root-classpath loading); deliverable is a written recommendation and, if needed, a small proof of concept - no production code.",
    "U3/U8 CI: configure CI plans (Maven-based) that trigger on every commit, run unit and integration tests, publish snapshots/artifacts to a repository, and notify on failures.",
    "Build with Maven (multi-module for s-c-s-m); testing with JUnit, Spring Test, and MockMvc for the REST layer; embedded/in-memory infrastructure used in tests where feasible (e.g., embedded Redis)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (the estimator) performs all work; estimates are effort (work-hours), not elapsed calendar time, and include design, implementation, unit/integration tests, and developer documentation for each activity.",
    "The s-c-d, s-c-s, and spring-cloud-stream-modules repositories already exist with basic project scaffolding; no greenfield repository or legal/open-source setup work is required.",
    "A CI server instance (e.g., Jenkins/Concourse/Bamboo) and the necessary credentials and permissions are available; no procurement or server installation effort is included.",
    "A Redis instance (or embedded Redis) is available for development and integration testing of the counter module.",
    "The U6 spike is validated via design analysis and a local proof of concept; access to a full PHD/HDFS cluster is not required.",
    "No UI work is in scope; the increment covers the REST API, the shell client, module ports/adaptations, launcher work, and CI only.",
    "Stories U1-U8 constitute the complete software increment; no additional features or hardening beyond what is listed is included.",
    "The technology baseline is the one implied by the stories (Spring Boot, Spring Cloud Stream/Data, Spring Shell, Spring Data Redis). The generic Spring Framework 6.0 / Java 17 note in the specification does not materially change the estimates.",
    "Code review happens within the activities; a final cross-story integration and verification activity is included separately."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Design shell and REST client approach",
      "activity_description": "Choose Spring Shell version, design command model for stream operations, and set up the HATEOAS-aware REST client (authentication, root-resource discovery, error mapping) used by the shell to invoke StreamController operations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement stream shell commands",
      "activity_description": "Implement shell commands for stream create/define, deploy, undeploy, destroy, list, and status, including argument/option handling, tab-completion hints, and formatted output of server responses.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Shell integration tests and docs",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests that run the shell against a live s-c-d server to validate StreamController operations end-to-end, plus user-facing command documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.1",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Analyze XD redis counter and design s-c-s module",
      "activity_description": "Review the Spring XD redis counter implementation (options, semantics, Redis usage) and design the equivalent spring-cloud-stream module: binder binding, configuration properties, and counter update/retrieve semantics for dashboard feeding.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement redis counter module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the standalone Spring Boot counter module using spring-cloud-stream binder abstraction and Spring Data Redis, including configuration properties and counter store/service logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Counter module tests and docs",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests (embedded/local Redis, binder test support) verifying counting semantics, and add module metadata/README documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.1",
      "activity_name": "U3 - CI pipeline for spring-cloud-data repo",
      "activity_description": "Configure the CI plan for the s-c-d repository: build triggered on every commit, Maven build with unit/integration test execution and reporting, artifact publishing to the snapshot repository, and failure notifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.1",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Design external-dependency loading approach",
      "activity_description": "Research and design how module-dependent JARs (e.g., database drivers) are resolved (Maven coordinates) and added to the launched module's classpath via a Boot loader extension, without embedding them in OOTB module archives.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.2",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Implement loader/resolver changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement the module resolver and Boot loader (PropertiesLauncher-style) changes that resolve dependent JARs at launch time and construct the module classloader accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.3",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Tests with sample external JAR and docs",
      "activity_description": "Verify the approach with a representative external dependency (e.g., a JDBC driver) via integration tests, and document how operators declare module dependencies.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.1",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Bootify ModuleLauncher core",
      "activity_description": "Refactor ModuleLauncher into a Spring Boot application: auto-configuration, @ConfigurationProperties with relaxed binding for module and launcher settings, replacing manual option parsing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.2",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Migrate option handling and tests",
      "activity_description": "Migrate existing module launch option handling to Boot property binding, preserve backward-compatible behavior, and update/add unit and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.1",
      "activity_name": "U6 - PHD/HDFS provider investigation spike",
      "activity_description": "Time-boxed investigation of approaches for supporting the HDFS module with PHD as provider: analyze classloader isolation, dependency shading, and root-classpath loading options; build a small proof of concept; document findings and a recommendation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.1",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Design stream REST API",
      "activity_description": "Define REST resources, URIs, representations, and HATEOAS links for stream commands (create/define, deploy, undeploy, destroy, list, status) and the error model, consistent with s-c-d API conventions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.2",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Implement StreamController",
      "activity_description": "Implement the StreamController @RestController endpoints backed by stream definition and deployment services, including request validation, resource assemblers, pagination for list, and exception handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.3",
      "activity_name": "U7 - REST tests and API documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write MockMvc and integration tests covering success and error paths for all stream endpoints, and produce REST API documentation (endpoints, payloads, examples).",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.1",
      "activity_name": "U8 - CI pipeline for spring-cloud-stream-modules repo",
      "activity_description": "Configure the CI plan for the multi-module s-c-s-m repository: per-commit Maven builds across all modules, test execution and reporting, per-module artifact publishing, and failure notifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9.1",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting - Final integration and verification",
      "activity_description": "Cross-story integration: verify shell against the new REST API end-to-end, run full builds on both CI pipelines, resolve integration issues, and perform final code review and release-readiness checks for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 284
  }
}
